{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "bookCode": "RV10",
  "bookSlug": "rig-veda-book-10",
  "n": 189,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "refId": "RV10-189:1",
      "text": "translated by"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "refId": "RV10-189:2",
      "text": "1. THIS spotted Bull hath come, and sat before the Mother in the east,",
      "original": "आयं गौः पृश्निरक्रमीदसदन्मातरं पुरः ।",
      "translit": "āyaṃ gauḥ pṛśnirakramīdasadanmātaraṃ puraḥ |"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "refId": "RV10-189:3",
      "text": "Advancing to his Father heaven.",
      "original": "पितरं च प्रयन्स्वः",
      "translit": "pitaraṃ ca prayansvaḥ"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "refId": "RV10-189:4",
      "text": "2. Expiring when he draws his breath, she moves along the lucid spheres:",
      "original": "अन्तश्चरति रोचनास्य प्राणादपानती ।",
      "translit": "antaścarati rocanāsya prāṇādapānatī |"
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "refId": "RV10-189:5",
      "text": "The Bull shines out through all the sky.",
      "original": "व्यख्यन्महिषो दिवम्",
      "translit": "vyakhyanmahiṣo divam"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "refId": "RV10-189:6",
      "text": "3. Song is bestowed upon the Bird: it rules supreme through thirty realms",
      "original": "त्रिंशद्धाम वि राजति वाक्पतंगाय धीयते ।",
      "translit": "triṃśaddhāma vi rājati vākpataṃgāya dhīyate |"
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "refId": "RV10-189:7",
      "text": "Throughout the days at break of morn.",
      "original": "प्रति वस्तोरह द्युभिः",
      "translit": "prati vastoraha dyubhiḥ"
    }
  ]
}
